  <!-- Section 1: Late 2026 Pricing Breakdown -->
  <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-black text-gray-950 mt-12 mb-4 tracking-tight">
    1. Late 2026 Tesla Supercharger Pricing Breakdown (US Averages &amp; Tiers)
  </h2>
  <p class="mb-4 leading-relaxed">
    Unlike residential electricity, which is heavily regulated by state public utility commissions (PUCs), Tesla operates Superchargers as a dynamic commercial service. Rates vary by location, local utility demand charges, time of day (Time-of-Use / TOU), and driver vehicle brand.
  </p>

  <p class="mb-6 leading-relaxed">
    Across more than 2,200 Supercharger stations in the US, pricing in late 2026 is divided into four distinct operational tiers:
  </p>

  <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 my-8 not-prose">
    <!-- Card 1 -->
    <div class="p-5 bg-white border-2 border-gray-200 rounded-2xl shadow-xs">
      <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-2">
        <span class="px-2.5 py-0.5 rounded-md text-[10px] font-black uppercase bg-emerald-100 text-emerald-900">Member Tier</span>
        <span class="text-xs font-bold text-gray-500">Tesla Owners &amp; Subscribers</span>
      </div>
      <h3 class="text-base font-black text-gray-950 mb-1">$0.40 to $0.43 / kWh (US Average)</h3>
      <p class="text-xs text-gray-600 mb-3 leading-relaxed">
        Applies automatically to all Tesla vehicle owners (Model 3, Model Y, Model S, Model X, Cybertruck) and non-Tesla EV owners who subscribe to the $12.99/month Supercharging membership.
      </p>
      <div class="pt-3 border-t border-gray-100 text-xs font-semibold text-gray-800">
        <div>Off-Peak Window (10 PM – 8 AM): <span class="text-emerald-700 font-black">$0.30–$0.36 / kWh</span></div>
        <div class="text-[11px] text-gray-500 mt-0.5">Approx. 11.4¢ to 12.3¢ per mile at 3.5 mi/kWh efficiency.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Card 2 -->
    <div class="p-5 bg-white border-2 border-gray-200 rounded-2xl shadow-xs">
      <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-2">
        <span class="px-2.5 py-0.5 rounded-md text-[10px] font-black uppercase bg-amber-100 text-amber-900">Non-Member Tier</span>
        <span class="text-xs font-bold text-gray-500">Pay-As-You-Go (PAYG)</span>
      </div>
      <h3 class="text-base font-black text-gray-950 mb-1">$0.57 to $0.60 / kWh (US Average)</h3>
      <p class="text-xs text-gray-600 mb-3 leading-relaxed">
        Applies to Ford, GM (<a href="/blog/chevy-equinox-ev-charging-cost-at-home-us" class="text-emerald-700 font-bold hover:underline">Chevy Equinox EV</a>, Blazer EV), Rivian, and other non-Tesla EV drivers who do not maintain an active $12.99 monthly membership.
      </p>
      <div class="pt-3 border-t border-gray-100 text-xs font-semibold text-gray-800">
        <div>Peak Urban Windows (12 PM – 8 PM): <span class="text-red-700 font-black">$0.63–$0.72+ / kWh</span></div>
        <div class="text-[11px] text-gray-500 mt-0.5">Approx. 16.3¢ to 17.1¢ per mile (surpassing gas costs).</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Card 3 -->
    <div class="p-5 bg-white border-2 border-gray-200 rounded-2xl shadow-xs">
