    Some prospective EV buyers worry that commercial fast-charging prices ruin the economic premise of an electric vehicle. But this fear misunderstands how electric cars are energized in daily life.
  </p>

  <p class="mb-4 leading-relaxed">
    Unlike combustion vehicle drivers who must visit a retail gas station every week, EV drivers wake up every morning with a "full tank" replenished overnight in their own garage or driveway. Telemetry from the US Department of Energy demonstrates that American EV owners perform over <strong>85% of their total charging at home</strong>, relying on public DC fast chargers for only <strong>10% to 15% of annual driving</strong> (primarily during long weekend trips and vacations).
