  <!-- Section 5: Step by Step Access -->
  <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-black text-gray-950 mt-12 mb-4 tracking-tight">
    5. Step-by-Step: How Non-Tesla Drivers Access &amp; Pay at Superchargers
  </h2>
  <p class="mb-6 leading-relaxed">
    If you own a Ford, GM, Rivian, Hyundai, or Kia EV, charging at a Tesla Supercharger in late 2026 is seamless if you follow these four steps:
  </p>

  <div class="space-y-4 my-8 not-prose">
    <div class="p-5 rounded-2xl bg-white border border-gray-200 shadow-xs flex items-start gap-3.5">
      <span class="w-8 h-8 rounded-xl bg-gray-950 text-white flex items-center justify-center font-black text-sm shrink-0">1</span>
      <div>
        <strong class="text-sm sm:text-base font-black text-gray-950 block mb-0.5">Download the Tesla App &amp; Add Payment</strong>
        <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-gray-600 leading-relaxed font-medium">
          Create an account in the official Tesla mobile app (iOS or Android) and store a default payment method. Under the menu, select <em>Charge Your Other EV</em>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="p-5 rounded-2xl bg-white border border-gray-200 shadow-xs flex items-start gap-3.5">
      <span class="w-8 h-8 rounded-xl bg-gray-950 text-white flex items-center justify-center font-black text-sm shrink-0">2</span>
      <div>
        <strong class="text-sm sm:text-base font-black text-gray-950 block mb-0.5">Filter for NACS-Compatible V3 &amp; V4 Stalls</strong>
        <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-gray-600 leading-relaxed font-medium">
          Only Tesla V3 (250 kW) and V4 (350 kW) stalls support CCS1 adapters. Older V2 stalls (150 kW with dual silver charging cables) communicate via proprietary CAN bus protocols and cannot talk to non-Tesla CCS vehicles.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="p-5 rounded-2xl bg-white border border-gray-200 shadow-xs flex items-start gap-3.5">
      <span class="w-8 h-8 rounded-xl bg-gray-950 text-white flex items-center justify-center font-black text-sm shrink-0">3</span>
