        <strong class="text-sm sm:text-base font-black text-gray-950 block mb-0.5">Attach Approved OEM NACS Adapter Securely</strong>
        <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-gray-600 leading-relaxed font-medium">
          Click the Tesla Supercharger connector firmly into your OEM NACS-to-CCS1 adapter until the mechanical latch engages, then plug the adapter into your vehicle's charge port.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="p-5 rounded-2xl bg-white border border-gray-200 shadow-xs flex items-start gap-3.5">
      <span class="w-8 h-8 rounded-xl bg-gray-950 text-white flex items-center justify-center font-black text-sm shrink-0">4</span>
      <div>
        <strong class="text-sm sm:text-base font-black text-gray-950 block mb-0.5">Activate via App or Native Plug &amp; Charge</strong>
        <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-gray-600 leading-relaxed font-medium">
          For vehicles equipped with native ISO 15118 Plug &amp; Charge (like Ford and GM), the session starts automatically. Otherwise, select the stall number (e.g., 3B) inside the Tesla app and press <em>Start Charging</em>.
        </p>
